 Steam Age

Purpose

The Steam Age is the first true industrial age.

The player transitions from primitive processing to powered machinery and continuous production.

Steam provides the first reliable industrial power system and introduces meaningful automation, larger production chains, and specialized machinery.

The Steam Age establishes the foundation for all later technological progression.

## Resources

The Steam Age primarily uses:

Iron
Copper
Tin
Zinc
Coal
Redstone
Steel
Bronze
Brass
Rubber
Other materials required for Steam-tier machinery

Resources from higher technological tiers may exist in the world, but their advanced applications remain locked.

Tools

The player gains access to the first industrial tools and equipment.

Tools available during the Steam Age should improve resource gathering and industrial construction without providing capabilities intended for later technological tiers.

Personal equipment must remain secondary to the development of industrial infrastructure.

Processing

Steam introduces the first significant increase in processing efficiency.

Production chains should begin requiring multiple stages of processing.

Examples include:

Raw Material
    ↓
Basic Processing
    ↓
Intermediate Material
    ↓
Industrial Component
    ↓
Machine Component
```

The player should begin transitioning from individual crafting to continuous production.

Steam-powered processing should be substantially more efficient than Primitive processing, while remaining far below the capabilities of electrical tiers.

## Machines

The Steam Age introduces the first major industrial machines.

Machines should include systems for:

Material processing
Mechanical production
Steam-powered processing
Component manufacturing
Resource preparation
Basic industrial automation

Machines from GregTech, Modern Industrialization, and Create should have distinct roles rather than simply providing multiple versions of the same machine.

Steam machinery should form the foundation for later electrical machines.

Power

Steam is the primary industrial power system of this age.

The player must establish a reliable steam infrastructure consisting of:

Fuel production
Water supply
Steam generation
Steam distribution
Steam-powered machinery

Steam production should require meaningful infrastructure rather than functioning as a single isolated machine.

Increasing industrial capacity should require expanding the steam system.

Automation

The Steam Age introduces significant automation.

The player should be able to create continuous production lines for common materials and components.

Automation may include:

Automated resource processing
Automated material transport
Automated machine inputs and outputs
Multi-machine production lines
Basic resource buffering
Continuous steam-powered production

However, automation remains constrained by steam production and machine throughput.

The player should need to design and expand their industrial infrastructure rather than simply placing a single machine.

Create Integration

Create should provide the mechanical infrastructure of the Steam Age.

Create systems may be used for:

Mechanical power transmission
Item transportation
Mechanical processing
Factory construction
Material handling
Early automation

Create should complement GregTech and Modern Industrialization rather than bypass their progression.

Create automation must not provide an alternative route around technological gates.

GregTech Integration

GregTech provides the primary structured technological progression of the Steam Age.

GregTech materials and processing chains should establish the requirements for advancing toward LV.

Steam-era GregTech progression should encourage the player to build increasingly organized production infrastructure.

GregTech should define the technological requirements while other industrial mods provide complementary systems.

Modern Industrialization Integration

Modern Industrialization provides additional machinery and production systems that complement the Steam Age.

Its machines and materials should be integrated into the same progression rather than creating an independent technological path.

Modern Industrialization should provide useful alternatives or specialized production capabilities without allowing the player to bypass the primary progression.

Requirements

The player must complete the Primitive Age before entering the Steam Age.

The player should have:

Completed primitive material processing
Established a stable supply of basic resources
Produced the components required for Steam machinery
Established a reliable water supply
Established a fuel supply
Built the infrastructure required for steam generation

## Exit Condition

The Steam Age ends when the player has developed a sufficiently advanced steam-powered industrial infrastructure to transition into electrical technology.

The player must:

Establish reliable large-scale steam production
Automate the production of essential materials
Complete the required Steam-tier production chains
Produce the components required for the first electrical machines
Establish the infrastructure required to begin LV progression

The completion of these requirements unlocks the LV tier.

The Steam Age should leave the player with a functioning industrial base rather than simply a collection of machines.
